# INCLUDE-PATTERN WHITELIST (owner directive): everything not listed here is
# kept OUT of the build context, so VCS, build outputs, the test262 checkout
# and host binaries/artifacts never enter any image. Line 1 excludes the
# world; the ! lines re-admit exactly what the build consumes (the same set
# build.sh's TREE_NEEDS names, plus docker/ and the PGO data). Re-exclude
# compiler artifacts afterwards: inside admitted directories a host-built
# *.a/*.o/*.so must never leak into an image (an arm64 archive cannot link
# in an amd64 image — that bug is why the artifact rules exist).
*
!build.sh
!VERSION
!.build-variant
!repl.js
!repl.c
!dynajs.d.ts
!install.sh
!README.md
!src
!tests
!third_party
!tools
!examples
!bench
!docker
!pgo-data
!hello.c
!test_fib.c
**/*.o
**/*.d
**/*.a
**/*.so
dynajs
dynajsc
dynajs-debug
run-test262
run-test262-debug
host-dynajsc
